# `**/` on every one of these, and it is not a flourish.
#
# A `.dockerignore` pattern is matched against the path from the context root, so a bare
# `node_modules` excludes `/node_modules` and NOTHING ELSE. Since 10i there is a second npm
# project at `web/`, and without the prefix its `node_modules` — a few hundred megabytes of
# Next and its transitive dependencies — was copied into the build context, sent to the
# daemon, and then copied over by `npm ci` in the stage that needs it.
#
# `web/.next` and `web/out` are the same hazard with a worse ending: a stale export from
# somebody's laptop, copied in and then overwritten by the build, or not.
**/node_modules
.git
test
docs
*.md
web/.next
web/out
